03:28:30,580 --> 03:28:32,580
Sony Sony Sony!

4499
03:28:32,580 --> 03:28:34,380
Okay okay okay!

4500
03:28:34,380 --> 03:28:36,180
Whoa!

4501
03:29:05,980 --> 03:29:07,980
Why?

4502
03:29:09,980 --> 03:29:11,980
Watch out! Watch out!

4503
03:29:13,980 --> 03:29:15,980
Watch out!

4504
03:29:15,980 --> 03:29:17,980
Run! Run!

4505
03:29:17,980 --> 03:29:19,980
We're not friends!

4506
03:29:19,980 --> 03:29:21,980
We're friends, aren't we?!

4507
03:29:21,980 --> 03:29:23,980
We're not friends!

4508
03:29:24,980 --> 03:29:26,980
Come quietly!

4509
03:29:30,980 --> 03:29:33,980
It's not like we did anything wrong!

4510
03:29:33,980 --> 03:29:35,980
We did! All kinds of stuff!

4511
03:29:36,980 --> 03:29:39,980
I didn't kill anyone! I swear!

4512
03:29:39,980 --> 03:29:41,980
What are you talking about?!

4513
03:29:41,980 --> 03:29:44,980
It was the brother, right? The brother's thing?

4514
03:29:44,980 --> 03:29:46,980
It's not just the brother!

4515
03:29:46,980 --> 03:29:48,980
We've piled up way too much at this point!

4516
03:29:49,980 --> 03:29:51,980
Aren't we in this together?!

4517
03:29:53,980 --> 03:29:55,980
I'm fine with it!

4518
03:29:55,980 --> 03:29:57,980
I'm fine with it!

4519
03:29:58,980 --> 03:29:59,980
You can't just say you're fine with it!

4520
03:29:59,980 --> 03:30:01,980
Can't be helped!

4521
03:30:02,980 --> 03:30:04,280
Heh~

4522
03:30:05,580 --> 03:30:08,580
Where are you, Miko Miko?

4523
03:30:08,580 --> 03:30:11,280
No! No! Yes!

4524
03:30:11,980 --> 03:30:12,980
No!

4525
03:30:12,980 --> 03:30:16,480
Hello, Miko Miko!

4526
03:30:16,480 --> 03:30:18,980
Hmm, goodbye, Korone!

4527
03:30:18,980 --> 03:30:20,980
Hey! Aah!

4528
03:30:20,980 --> 03:30:22,980
That's awful! Ugh, this...

4529
03:30:22,980 --> 03:30:25,980
Gender equality is Miko's policy, you know!

4530
03:30:25,980 --> 03:30:30,480
That's it! That's it! What was it called? Isn't that obstruction of justice or something?

4531
03:30:30,480 --> 03:30:31,980
No! Yes!

4532
03:30:31,980 --> 03:30:33,980
We've got nothing left to lose!

4533
03:30:36,980 --> 03:30:37,980
There!

4534
03:30:37,980 --> 03:30:38,980
Take that!

4535
03:30:39,980 --> 03:30:40,980
Ha!

4536
03:30:42,980 --> 03:30:43,980
Ngh!

4537
03:30:47,980 --> 03:30:48,980
Hmm...

4538
03:30:48,980 --> 03:30:52,980
Obstruction of business! Obstruction of business!

4539
03:30:52,980 --> 03:30:54,980
This is obstruction of business!

4540
03:30:54,980 --> 03:30:56,980
Obstruction of business!

4541
03:30:58,980 --> 03:31:00,980
She's not dead!

4542
03:31:01,980 --> 03:31:02,520
Ultraman!

4543
03:31:12,660 --> 03:31:16,260
Don't go saying my name!

4544
03:31:19,920 --> 03:31:21,860
Take this!

4545
03:31:21,860 --> 03:31:23,660
Wait, what is this?!

4546
03:31:23,660 --> 03:31:25,460
What is this?! What is this?!

4547
03:31:25,460 --> 03:31:27,460
What is this?! What's going on?!

4548
03:31:27,460 --> 03:31:33,940
Huh?

4549
03:31:33,940 --> 03:31:35,740
So like...

4550
03:31:35,740 --> 03:31:37,540
It looks like we really

4551
03:31:37,540 --> 03:31:39,470
have to fight each other.

4552
03:31:39,470 --> 03:31:41,140
Seriously?

4553
03:31:41,140 --> 03:31:43,940
No way! Miko Miko!

4554
03:31:43,940 --> 03:31:44,940
It's true.

4555
03:31:44,940 --> 03:31:47,740
Truth is, I always loved Miko Miko.

4556
03:31:48,720 --> 03:31:50,540
I knew it.

4557
03:31:50,540 --> 03:31:52,340
I loved you too,

4558
03:31:52,340 --> 03:31:54,130
but

4559
03:32:01,770 --> 03:32:03,770
I've got a son waiting for me.

4560
03:32:06,840 --> 03:32:08,840
Whoa, what is this?!

4561
03:32:10,970 --> 03:32:12,970
Is this it?

4562
03:32:12,970 --> 03:32:14,770
Stop, stop, stop!

4563
03:32:14,770 --> 03:32:16,570
Please stop!

4564
03:32:16,570 --> 03:32:18,580
Hey!

4565
03:32:18,580 --> 03:32:20,480
Miko! Miko!

4566
03:32:20,480 --> 03:32:22,180
What?

4567
03:32:22,180 --> 03:32:24,180
Let's talk this out!

4568
03:32:24,180 --> 03:32:25,780
Fine.

4569
03:32:25,780 --> 03:32:27,580
Over here? He said something.

4570
03:32:27,580 --> 03:32:28,530
Where are you?

4571
03:32:28,530 --> 03:32:30,270
Show your face!

4572
03:32:38,750 --> 03:32:40,550
Miko! Miko!

4573
03:32:42,350 --> 03:32:44,350
No, wait, wait, wait!

4574
03:32:46,150 --> 03:32:47,150
Yeah!

4575
03:32:47,950 --> 03:32:49,780
Mika! Mika!

4576
03:32:49,780 --> 03:32:50,750
Ow!

4577
03:32:50,750 --> 03:32:51,550
Ow!

4578
03:32:52,350 --> 03:32:53,350
Ow!

4579
03:32:54,150 --> 03:32:55,150
That hurts!

4580
03:32:56,000 --> 03:32:57,950
This hurts!

4581
03:32:57,950 --> 03:33:00,640
Where does it hurt? Your heart?

4582
03:33:00,640 --> 03:33:04,550
My heart hurts AND it physically hurts!

4583
03:33:11,980 --> 03:33:13,780
You're all over the place!

4584
03:33:14,780 --> 03:33:16,580
Yeah, it's definitely hitting!

4585
03:33:17,380 --> 03:33:18,380
How about that!

4586
03:33:19,180 --> 03:33:20,180
Oh no!

4587
03:33:25,630 --> 03:33:27,630
You were acting all righteous!

4588
03:33:28,430 --> 03:33:31,430
You two are brothers already!

4589
03:33:36,470 --> 03:33:38,270
Why though!

4590
03:33:39,180 --> 03:33:41,070
Drop the gun!

4591
03:33:45,670 --> 03:33:47,670
We're on the same side!

4592
03:34:03,470 --> 03:34:04,770
Does it hurt?

4593
03:34:04,770 --> 03:34:06,770
Ow!

4594
03:34:13,730 --> 03:34:15,730
Huh? Miko, Miko, where are you?

4595
03:34:15,730 --> 03:34:17,470
Anywhere.

4596
03:34:17,470 --> 03:34:19,130
You're not there?

4597
03:34:19,130 --> 03:34:21,560
I'm not there.

4598
03:34:21,560 --> 03:34:23,560
Oh, Miko, Miko?

4599
03:34:23,560 --> 03:34:25,360
I'm not there!

4600
03:34:27,160 --> 03:34:29,160
Let's be friends!

4601
03:34:30,760 --> 03:34:32,760
I'm not there!

4602
03:34:36,500 --> 03:34:38,500
I'm gonna die soon!

4603
03:34:40,080 --> 03:34:42,080
Omiko! Omiko!

4604
03:34:42,600 --> 03:34:45,540
Hey, let's talk it out?

4605
03:34:48,000 --> 03:34:51,000
I'm gonna die, Omiko, Omiko! Ah...

4606
03:34:51,420 --> 03:34:54,200
Huh? Oh? A fistfight?

4607
03:34:54,000 --> 03:34:55,800
In the end—

4608
03:34:57,600 --> 03:34:58,400
Aah!

4609
03:34:58,400 --> 03:35:02,200
Wah, wah, wah— it's like Mewtwo. Like Mewtwo Strikes Back.

4610
03:35:04,000 --> 03:35:06,000
Pikachu!

4611
03:35:07,800 --> 03:35:09,800
Pikachu!

4612
03:35:10,600 --> 03:35:11,600
Pikachu!

4613
03:35:11,600 --> 03:35:12,590
No!

4614
03:35:13,390 --> 03:35:16,100
Stop with the Pikachu stuff!

4615
03:35:17,110 --> 03:35:18,910
Don't cry!

4616
03:35:18,910 --> 03:35:21,710
Niko doesn't want to do this!

4617
03:35:21,710 --> 03:35:24,510
I've been betrayed so many times.

4618
03:35:25,360 --> 03:35:26,970
Even bugs grew on me.

4619
03:35:26,970 --> 03:35:29,110
I even saw you naked.

4620
03:35:29,110 --> 03:35:31,490
And yet—

4621
03:35:31,490 --> 03:35:33,910
Why would you do this—

4622
03:35:33,910 --> 03:35:36,070
Ow!

4623
03:35:36,070 --> 03:35:38,290
Hey, stop, not that—

4624
03:35:38,290 --> 03:35:41,010
Stop that!

4625
03:35:41,010 --> 03:35:42,670
That's not okay!

4626
03:35:42,670 --> 03:35:46,150
That's cheating!

4627
03:35:46,150 --> 03:35:47,410
That hurts!

4628
03:35:47,410 --> 03:35:49,840
That's not fair!

4629
03:35:52,620 --> 03:35:54,820
I can't do that!

4630
03:35:54,820 --> 03:35:59,120
I have a family!

4631
03:36:06,910 --> 03:36:12,530
Look at my HP! I'm about to die!

4632
03:36:12,330 --> 03:36:14,330
Ahahahaha!

4633
03:36:15,330 --> 03:36:16,330
Hmm~

4634
03:36:18,330 --> 03:36:19,330
No.

4635
03:36:20,330 --> 03:36:21,330
No~

4636
03:36:22,330 --> 03:36:26,330
But I have Alex!

4637
03:36:27,330 --> 03:36:28,330
Alex?

4638
03:36:28,330 --> 03:36:30,330
Hey, I don't know about that! I don't know about that!

4639
03:36:30,330 --> 03:36:32,330
Don't bring up stuff I don't know about!

4640
03:36:33,330 --> 03:36:36,330
Hey~ that's stuff I don't know about!

4641
03:36:37,330 --> 03:36:39,330
Ahh, we're gonna die watching this!

4642
03:36:39,330 --> 03:36:41,330
It's a soma light! (Souma Akari)

4643
03:36:42,330 --> 03:36:44,330
Ahhhhh!

4644
03:36:44,330 --> 03:36:46,330
Ahhhhh!

4645
03:36:46,330 --> 03:36:48,330
Ahhhhh!

4646
03:36:48,330 --> 03:36:50,330
I know that one!

4647
03:36:50,330 --> 03:36:52,330
No you don't!

4648
03:36:52,330 --> 03:36:54,330
You definitely don't!

4649
03:36:54,330 --> 03:36:56,330
Why do you know it before me?!

4650
03:36:58,330 --> 03:37:00,330
Heeey!

4651
03:37:00,330 --> 03:37:02,330
We're gonna die!

4652
03:37:06,330 --> 03:37:08,330
I don't wanna do this! I'll flip it!

4653
03:37:08,330 --> 03:37:10,330
We can do it this way!

4654
03:37:10,330 --> 03:37:12,330
Why?

4655
03:37:12,330 --> 03:37:13,330
What are you looking at?

4656
03:37:13,330 --> 03:37:15,330
You're the one looking at it!

4657
03:37:17,330 --> 03:37:19,330
Ready, steady—

4658
03:37:19,330 --> 03:37:22,330
Steady... go!

4659
03:37:29,330 --> 03:37:32,330
Come on, try it!

4660
03:37:33,330 --> 03:37:36,330
Try catching up to me!

4661
03:37:38,330 --> 03:37:41,150
How does that feel?!

4662
03:38:10,950 --> 03:38:11,330
Thank you very much!

4663
03:38:11,150 --> 03:38:14,710
Thank you for watching!

4664
03:38:14,510 --> 03:38:24,510
This is more... oh, mecha mecha. Sorry for talking during the cutscene. Ow! Mecha mecha. Mecha mecha.

4665
03:38:31,510 --> 03:38:33,930
Whoa, uwah—

4666
03:38:33,930 --> 03:38:43,930
Boo boo, it's going in, going in, going in... I can't get out, I can't do it, but go ahead—

4667
03:38:44,110 --> 03:38:47,330
The venue, the venue, the performance—

4668
03:38:48,430 --> 03:38:50,750
Pfft—

4669
03:38:51,490 --> 03:38:55,390
This, like... right now, like—

4670
03:38:55,390 --> 03:39:00,210
Pff— sorry for talking in the middle of it!

4671
03:39:00,210 --> 03:39:04,610
I really couldn't forgive that back then!

4672
03:39:04,610 --> 03:39:05,610
Ugh, this is such a pain!

4673
03:39:07,010 --> 03:39:10,610
Ahh, this is so sad!

4674
03:39:13,010 --> 03:39:15,010
What is this?

4675
03:39:16,210 --> 03:39:17,010
Leo!

4676
03:39:19,410 --> 03:39:21,010
Leooo!

4677
03:39:23,910 --> 03:39:25,010
Leooo!

4678
03:39:25,010 --> 03:39:27,810
This is way too painful!

4679
03:39:30,210 --> 03:39:32,930
This is rough...

4680
03:39:32,930 --> 03:39:36,310
This is rough...

4681
03:39:36,310 --> 03:39:38,550
So rough...

4682
03:39:38,550 --> 03:39:40,590
This is intense.

4683
03:39:40,590 --> 03:39:43,790
Holding hands at the end — that's not fair!

4684
03:39:43,790 --> 03:39:47,390
This is intense, huh.

4685
03:39:53,830 --> 03:39:57,610
Man, this is just incredible...

4686
03:39:57,610 --> 03:40:04,910
Wait, is he going to tell her?

4687
03:40:04,910 --> 03:40:06,450
His family?

4688
03:40:06,450 --> 03:40:08,230
No wait, seriously—

4689
03:40:08,230 --> 03:40:10,410
Miko is already crying.

4690
03:40:10,410 --> 03:40:12,830
Whoa, she came—

4691
03:40:12,830 --> 03:40:14,910
It's not cheating, it's not cheating!

4692
03:40:14,510 --> 03:40:16,510
Is that you?

4693
03:40:31,510 --> 03:40:34,510
Go play with the kids. — Okay.

4694
03:40:34,510 --> 03:40:37,510
Okay! Right, the three of them played together, didn't they?

4695
03:40:44,510 --> 03:40:48,510
She's not coming back!

4696
03:41:03,500 --> 03:41:05,060
This hurts...

4697
03:41:04,860 --> 03:41:08,460
It's about Leo.

4698
03:41:08,460 --> 03:41:09,920
What about him?

4699
03:41:50,860 --> 03:41:54,860
This is so painful...

4700
03:41:54,860 --> 03:41:57,860
So painful...

4701
03:41:57,860 --> 03:42:00,860
It's gonna make you go like... dun dun dun dun...

4702
03:42:00,860 --> 03:42:04,860
Hmm... Sudie!

4703
03:42:06,860 --> 03:42:08,860
Wassho!

4704
03:42:08,860 --> 03:42:10,860
Stop it!

4705
03:42:21,860 --> 03:42:24,860
Onee-chan!

4706
03:42:24,860 --> 03:42:26,860
Stop it, please!

4707
03:42:27,860 --> 03:42:31,120
Mama? Mama!

4708
03:42:34,120 --> 03:42:36,000
Oh my god!

4709
03:42:38,000 --> 03:42:42,860
This is crazy... this is crazy...

4710
03:42:50,960 --> 03:42:53,860
But you know, on the flip side—

4711
03:42:53,860 --> 03:42:58,820
If we had been the ones to die, they'd have to tell the wife who's holding the baby, right?

4712
03:43:01,380 --> 03:43:03,360
That would be rough too.

4713
03:43:03,360 --> 03:43:05,360
So there are two endings for this?

4714
03:43:06,080 --> 03:43:07,080
Yeah.

4715
03:43:17,580 --> 03:43:19,440
Oh, did he come home?

4716
03:43:38,070 --> 03:43:39,070
Oh, the baby!

4717
03:43:48,960 --> 03:43:50,000
A letter.

4718
03:43:50,000 --> 03:43:51,000
A letter.

4719
03:43:52,640 --> 03:43:54,640
A letter? A letter here?

4720
03:44:05,460 --> 03:44:07,260
Give me one more chance.

4721
03:44:10,160 --> 03:44:14,760
Apparently he quit the police force.

4722
03:44:18,360 --> 03:44:21,160
He must have been throwing himself into his work.

4723
03:44:27,810 --> 03:44:35,610
Leo advised him to write a letter, and he actually did it — what an idiot!

4724
03:44:35,610 --> 03:44:37,410
Idiot!

4725
03:44:43,700 --> 03:44:45,700
I love it too.

4726
03:44:45,500 --> 03:44:51,300
That's nice.

4727
03:44:51,300 --> 03:44:55,560
But still, it leaves me feeling a little unsettled.

4728
03:44:55,560 --> 03:45:02,300
Yeah, this one hits pretty hard.

4729
03:45:02,300 --> 03:45:04,920
But maybe it couldn't be helped.

4730
03:45:04,920 --> 03:45:07,680
Yeah, you're right.

4731
03:45:07,680 --> 03:45:12,200
It's rough.

4732
03:45:12,200 --> 03:45:16,200
Whoa! Leo leap!

4733
03:45:16,200 --> 03:45:18,200
No!

4734
03:45:22,200 --> 03:45:24,200
Recon leap!

4735
03:45:24,200 --> 03:45:26,200
No!

4736
03:45:26,200 --> 03:45:30,200
Ahhh!

4737
03:45:30,200 --> 03:45:34,200
The baby's not moving!

4738
03:45:38,200 --> 03:45:41,200
Leo!

4739
03:45:41,200 --> 03:45:45,840
Wow, this kid is tough.

4740
03:45:45,840 --> 03:45:49,880
Alex, you really take after your dad.

4741
03:45:49,880 --> 03:45:55,680
It was good that Alex said that.

4742
03:45:55,680 --> 03:45:56,700
Yeah.

4743
03:45:56,700 --> 03:45:59,280
Alex...

4744
03:46:11,200 --> 03:46:15,200
You've gotta protect your mom!

4745
03:46:15,200 --> 03:46:17,200
Oh no...

4746
03:46:21,200 --> 03:46:23,200
Somewhere...

4747
03:46:23,200 --> 03:46:26,200
Like, "I have to protect Mom."

4748
03:46:26,200 --> 03:46:27,200
Yeah.

4749
03:46:27,200 --> 03:46:28,200
It's hard to say.

4750
03:46:28,200 --> 03:46:29,200
Yeah.

4751
03:46:29,200 --> 03:46:31,200
Whoa!

4752
03:46:31,200 --> 03:46:34,200
This is just too much, seriously.

4753
03:46:34,200 --> 03:46:37,200
That was really fun though!

4754
03:46:37,200 --> 03:46:38,200
Yeah, it really was.

4755
03:46:38,200 --> 03:46:42,200
So, the first half was on Miko's channel,

4756
03:46:42,200 --> 03:46:45,900
we played it on the 4th, and this was the continuation from there.

4757
03:46:45,500 --> 03:46:46,460
From there...

4758
03:46:46,260 --> 03:46:48,720
And we managed to clear it!

4759
03:46:48,720 --> 03:46:50,730
Yay!

4760
03:46:50,730 --> 03:46:55,730
It really was like a movie.

4761
03:47:01,620 --> 03:47:05,700
Yeah, especially at the end.

4762
03:47:05,700 --> 03:47:10,140
I kept thinking they'd just get caught again no matter what.

4763
03:47:10,140 --> 03:47:11,140
Well, yeah.

4764
03:47:11,140 --> 03:47:13,020
But it ended up like this.

4765
03:47:13,020 --> 03:47:16,480
What a twist ending!

4766
03:47:16,480 --> 03:47:20,100
This was such an amazing game.

4767
03:47:20,100 --> 03:47:23,280
It was way beyond what I expected, honestly.

4768
03:47:23,280 --> 03:47:26,740
Playing through a second time knowing the ending would feel totally different.

4769
03:47:26,740 --> 03:47:27,620
You'd notice things from a completely different angle.

4770
03:47:27,620 --> 03:47:29,280
Yeah, totally.

4771
03:47:29,280 --> 03:47:32,220
Definitely worth playing again.

4772
03:47:32,220 --> 03:47:33,060
For sure.

4773
03:47:33,060 --> 03:47:36,000
Yeah, you could definitely enjoy it a second time.

4774
03:47:36,000 --> 03:47:39,080
I wonder if there's a true ending.

4775
03:47:39,080 --> 03:47:42,620
I think there might be two versions at the end.

4776
03:47:42,620 --> 03:47:46,100
Where one of them dies.

4777
03:47:46,100 --> 03:47:46,800
Like...?

4778
03:47:48,370 --> 03:47:49,800
That's what I was thinking.

4779
03:47:49,800 --> 03:47:54,530
So there really was a Leo ending too.

4780
03:47:54,530 --> 03:47:56,550
An ending where Leo survives.

4781
03:47:56,550 --> 03:47:58,690
But even if Leo survived,

4782
03:47:58,690 --> 03:48:00,230
he'd still get caught, right?

4783
03:48:00,230 --> 03:48:02,690
Yeah, probably.

4784
03:48:02,690 --> 03:48:04,730
He'd be pretty hunted down.

4785
03:48:04,730 --> 03:48:06,390
Whether you live or die —

4786
03:48:06,390 --> 03:48:08,750
there's quite a difference.

4787
03:48:08,750 --> 03:48:09,630
Right.

4788
03:48:09,630 --> 03:48:11,210
Dying is just so sad.

4789
03:48:11,210 --> 03:48:14,670
But you know,

4790
03:48:14,670 --> 03:48:16,110
at the very end,

4791
03:48:16,110 --> 03:48:19,190
that moment where they grabbed each other's hands —

4792
03:48:19,190 --> 03:48:26,290
it felt like all their feelings were really packed into that moment.

4793
03:48:26,290 --> 03:48:29,570
It wasn't just a simple betrayal at all.

4794
03:48:29,570 --> 03:48:35,470
There were clearly so many things that connected them.

4795
03:48:35,470 --> 03:48:44,650
But their circumstances meant they truly couldn't be friends with their whole hearts — that's just how it was.

4796
03:48:44,650 --> 03:48:47,410
They each had things they needed to protect.

4797
03:48:47,410 --> 03:48:52,190
On both sides.

4798
03:48:52,190 --> 03:48:57,390
It really came down to whose family you'd choose.

4799
03:48:57,390 --> 03:48:58,630
The title —

4800
03:48:58,630 --> 03:49:01,730
it means something like "escape" or "a way out," right?

4801
03:49:01,730 --> 03:49:02,630
Yeah, yeah.

4802
03:49:02,630 --> 03:49:03,690
So then—

4803
03:49:03,690 --> 03:49:06,090
If you put these together,

4804
03:49:06,090 --> 03:49:07,110
Mm-hmm.

4805
03:49:07,110 --> 03:49:09,270
does that mean it's just one?

4806
03:49:09,270 --> 03:49:11,110
Like, one way out?

4807
03:49:11,110 --> 03:49:12,710
Is that what it means?

4808
03:49:12,710 --> 03:49:14,510
What does it mean?

4809
03:49:14,510 --> 03:49:16,420
Is that right?

4810
03:49:16,420 --> 03:49:18,420
So it's just one.

4811
03:49:18,420 --> 03:49:20,420
But it's one or the other... I see.

4812
03:49:20,420 --> 03:49:22,220
So it's one or the other, huh.

4813
03:49:22,220 --> 03:49:24,220
Human author...

4814
03:49:24,220 --> 03:49:26,020
So it's for one person.

4815
03:49:34,430 --> 03:49:36,430
That's wild.

4816
03:49:36,430 --> 03:49:38,230
That was so much fun!

4817
03:49:38,230 --> 03:49:40,030
It really was!

4818
03:49:40,030 --> 03:49:41,980
I'm so glad we got to play together, Miko!

4819
03:49:41,980 --> 03:49:47,250
Yeah, I'm really glad we got to play together too, Korone! It was genuinely so fun.

4820
03:49:48,850 --> 03:49:50,740
Elite Miko, nyaa~

4821
03:49:50,740 --> 03:49:58,150
Right? But honestly, I really wanted to play this game with Korone specifically.

4822
03:49:58,150 --> 03:50:03,260
This collab made me want to play other games together too!

4823
03:50:03,260 --> 03:50:06,010
Yes! Thank you so much!

4824
03:50:06,010 --> 03:50:09,410
Please do check out the previous stream too!

4825
03:50:09,410 --> 03:50:11,910
Though the previous one is a bit... rated 18+,

4826
03:50:14,970 --> 03:50:16,970
That one's seriously wild.

4827
03:50:16,970 --> 03:50:20,470
Even though this one ended so nicely,

4828
03:50:20,470 --> 03:50:25,470
the first half of the previous stream is basically R18,

4829
03:50:25,470 --> 03:50:28,270
Yeah, that one was crazy too.

4830
03:50:28,270 --> 03:50:32,870
That was crazy — in a completely different way, though.

4831
03:50:32,870 --> 03:50:35,650
I was on the edge of my seat the whole time.

4832
03:50:35,650 --> 03:50:38,750
Like, "oh no, here it comes again"...

4833
03:50:38,750 --> 03:50:43,070
The previous one had me laughing so hard I thought I was going to die.

4834
03:50:43,070 --> 03:50:43,710
It was insane.

4835
03:50:43,710 --> 03:50:46,170
This one had emotion and intensity—

4836
03:50:46,170 --> 03:50:47,170
Yeah, yeah, exactly.

4837
03:50:47,170 --> 03:50:50,830
The twists just kept coming one after another!

4838
03:50:50,830 --> 03:50:52,830
It was incredible.

4839
03:50:52,830 --> 03:50:57,030
And once the ending credits finish, I'll be archiving this stream too,

4840
03:50:57,030 --> 03:50:57,530
Okay!

4841
03:50:57,530 --> 03:50:59,530
so please look forward to that.

4842
03:50:59,530 --> 03:51:00,330
Got it!

4843
03:51:00,330 --> 03:51:02,330
Miko, go ahead and read some comments!

4844
03:51:05,630 --> 03:51:08,730
Because of what we were just talking about, people are saying stuff like "Sausage Legend"...

4845
03:51:08,730 --> 03:51:12,730
This is not the right moment to be reading comments!

4846
03:51:13,530 --> 03:51:15,530
There are no comments to read right now!

4847
03:51:16,330 --> 03:51:18,330
That was a fail.

4848
03:51:18,330 --> 03:51:19,330
Yeah, that was a fail.

4849
03:51:19,330 --> 03:51:20,330
We messed up the timing.

4850
03:51:20,330 --> 03:51:21,330
The timing was off.

4851
03:51:23,130 --> 03:51:25,130
But it really was so much fun.

4852
03:51:25,130 --> 03:51:26,130
It really was!

4853
03:51:27,930 --> 03:51:30,910
This game is amazing.

4854
03:51:30,910 --> 03:51:34,130
I'm really curious about the other ending too.

4855
03:51:34,130 --> 03:51:35,370
Same!

4856
03:51:35,370 --> 03:51:39,590
Everyone, if you have a friend to play with, definitely give it a try!

4857
03:51:39,590 --> 03:51:39,990
Please do!

4858
03:51:39,990 --> 03:51:41,830
Can you play this solo?

4859
03:51:41,830 --> 03:51:44,270
Actually, you cannot play this one solo!

4860
03:51:44,270 --> 03:51:45,330
Oh, really?

4861
03:51:45,330 --> 03:51:45,950
Well, that makes sense.

4862
03:51:45,950 --> 03:51:47,750
You'd need like four hands otherwise.

4863
03:51:47,750 --> 03:51:48,510
Exactly, exactly.

4864
03:51:48,510 --> 03:51:52,030
You genuinely need another person to play this game.

4865
03:51:52,030 --> 03:51:53,330
Is that so?

4866
03:51:53,330 --> 03:51:54,910
Yep!

4867
03:51:54,910 --> 03:51:59,510
Oh, it's back to the title screen!

4868
03:51:59,510 --> 03:52:00,310
Yes!

4869
03:52:00,310 --> 03:52:04,310
Okay Miko, we've shared our thoughts, but

4870
03:52:04,310 --> 03:52:08,240
shall we each say one last thing before we wrap up?

4871
03:52:08,240 --> 03:52:09,060
Sure!

4872
03:52:09,060 --> 03:52:11,910
Will there be another Mikkorone collab?

4873
03:52:11,910 --> 03:52:14,510
Yes! There will!

4874
03:52:14,510 --> 03:52:18,110
We haven't nailed down a date yet, but—

4875
03:52:18,110 --> 03:52:19,110
There will be one, right?

4876
03:52:19,110 --> 03:52:25,610
Oh yeah, definitely, definitely! It'll be this month — wait, will it? Is this month okay?

4877
03:52:25,610 --> 03:52:34,210
Why, why?! No no, will it happen? Why? It will, right? It will? This month's Gust event will be gone again! You're right, let's do it, let's do it!

4878
03:52:34,210 --> 03:52:40,850
Is it definitely happening? Definitely? Let's go this year — come on! But hey, let's just do it every day!

4879
03:52:40,850 --> 03:52:42,930
Every day is a bit...

4880
03:52:42,930 --> 03:52:45,310
Every day is a bit much... Let's do it every day, every day!

4881
03:52:45,310 --> 03:52:48,610
Every day is a bit much... but everyone got left behind!

4882
03:52:48,610 --> 03:52:49,870
We got left behind!

4883
03:52:49,870 --> 03:52:53,710
But, like, we want to do Mikkorone streams regularly, right?

4884
03:52:53,710 --> 03:52:56,210
Yeah, we do! It was so fun!

4885
03:52:56,210 --> 03:52:57,710
Let's find another game to play!

4886
03:52:57,710 --> 03:52:58,710
Nooo~

4887
03:52:58,710 --> 03:53:00,510
Yay! So, with that—

4888
03:53:00,510 --> 03:53:03,660
Shall we wrap up for today? It got a little emotional there.

4889
03:53:03,660 --> 03:53:04,430
Yes.

4890
03:53:04,430 --> 03:53:08,910
It was so moving! Everyone, go ahead and wipe your tears with a tissue.

4891
03:53:08,910 --> 03:53:10,510
Yes.

4892
03:53:10,510 --> 03:53:12,310
Thank you so much!

4893
03:53:12,310 --> 03:53:15,110
Thank you so much!

4894
03:53:15,110 --> 03:53:16,910
See you again, good night!

4895
03:53:16,910 --> 03:53:20,700
Thank you!

4896
03:53:20,700 --> 03:53:21,700
Thank you, Miko too!

4897
03:53:21,700 --> 03:53:23,500
Thank you to all of Miko-P's fans too!

4898
03:53:23,500 --> 03:53:24,500
And all the Koronesuki!

4899
03:53:24,500 --> 03:53:25,500
Thank you!

4900
03:53:25,500 --> 03:53:27,300
All the Koronesuki!

4901
03:53:27,300 --> 03:53:28,300
Sorry for intruding!

4902
03:53:30,100 --> 03:53:31,100
Wait a second!

4903
03:53:31,100 --> 03:53:34,120
Hm?

4904
03:53:34,120 --> 03:53:36,120
Oh, bye~!

4905
03:53:39,540 --> 03:53:40,540
Huh?

4906
03:53:41,970 --> 03:53:43,270
Hold on!

4907
03:53:43,770 --> 03:53:50,030
That was such a perfect ending right there!
